---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="One simulated day. From 03:00 to 06:00 UTC a CDN fault makes the site slow for users in Brazil. Choose what watches the site and see who notices, and when.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>At the defaults (probe every 5 min from 3 locations, alert if any 1 fails, RUM at 10%) the synthetic checks <b>never</b> alert about the outage, because no probe runs in Brazil, and they raise 4 to 5 false alarms from single-probe blips. RUM alerts about 9 to 10 minutes after the start, but 500 to 600 Brazilian page views were already slow by then.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Probe locations</b> to 5 (the fifth is in Brazil): the probe sees the fault within 4 to 9 minutes. Now set <b>Failure rule</b> to 2 of 3: false alarms fall to 0, but only one location can fail, so the alert comes 18 to 120 minutes late (an unrelated blip has to join it) or never. Switch <b>Fault scope</b> to everywhere and the same rule alerts within 1 minute.</li>
    <li>With 5 locations and any 1 failing, compare intervals: every 1 min alerts at once but raises 22 to 26 false alarms in the day, every 15 min raises only 2 to 4 but alerts 12 minutes in.</li>
    <li>Set <b>RUM sampling</b> to 1%: RUM never alerts, because it cannot gather the 20 samples it needs in 15 minutes from a quiet night. Untick <b>Real user monitoring</b> with the defaults and nobody is alerted: all 7,170 slow page views happen before anyone knows.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg sm" data-sm>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Probe interval <select class="pg-in" data-interval><option value="1">every 1 min</option><option value="5" selected>every 5 min</option><option value="15">every 15 min</option></select></label>
      <RangeField label="Probe locations" name="locs" min="1" max="5" value="3" readout="3" />
      <label>Failure rule <select class="pg-in" data-rule><option value="1" selected>any 1 location</option><option value="2">2 of 3 locations</option><option value="3">3 of 5 locations</option></select></label>
      <label>Fault scope <select class="pg-in" data-scope><option value="brazil" selected>Brazil only</option><option value="global">everywhere</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note sm-locs" data-locnames></p>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label class="sm-check"><input type="checkbox" checked data-rumon /> Real user monitoring</label>
      <label>RUM sampling <select class="pg-in" data-sampling><option value="1">100% of page views</option><option value="0.25">25%</option><option value="0.1" selected>10%</option><option value="0.01">1%</option></select></label>
      <label>Day <select class="pg-in" data-seed><option value="1" selected>A</option><option value="2">B</option><option value="3">C</option></select></label>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Synthetic probes</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-sdet></span><span class="pg-note" data-sfa></span><span class="pg-note" data-schecks></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>Real user monitoring</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-rdet></span><span class="pg-note" data-rfa></span><span class="pg-note" data-rp75></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--bad)"><h3>Users hurt</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-hurt></span><span class="pg-note" data-hurtnote></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sm-chart" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Timeline of the simulated day with the outage band and alert markers">
      <svg class="sm-svg" viewBox="0 0 720 96" role="img" aria-label="Timeline from 00:00 to 24:00 UTC. A band marks the outage; filled dots are alerts that caught it, hollow dots are false alarms." data-svg></svg>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note sm-legend"><span class="sm-key sm-k1"></span> synthetic <span class="sm-key sm-k2"></span> RUM &nbsp; filled dot = caught the outage, hollow dot = false alarm, red band = outage</p>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: a probe in a faulted region fails 90% of the time; any probe also fails 0.4% of the time from a network blip; locations are staggered and the rule counts locations whose latest check failed. 12% of users block the RUM beacon. LCP is log-normal with a 1.7 s median (about 5.1 s during the fault); RUM alerts when the 15-minute p75 LCP of a region passes 4 s for 3 minutes in a row, needs 20 samples, and sees data 3 minutes late.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue, mulberry32 } from '../playground';
const DAY = 1440, FAULT_START = 180, FAULT_END = 360, BRAZIL = 4;
interface Params { seed: number; interval: number; locations: number; n: number; scope: string; rumOn: boolean; sampling: number }
  interface World { seed: number; blip: number[][]; fail: number[][] }
  interface Mark { t: number; kind: string }
  const REGIONS = [
  { id: 'us-east', name: 'US East', tz: -5, peak: 140 },
  { id: 'eu-west', name: 'EU West', tz: 0, peak: 120 },
  { id: 'ap-northeast', name: 'Tokyo', tz: 9, peak: 90 },
  { id: 'us-west', name: 'US West', tz: -8, peak: 80 },
  { id: 'sa-east', name: 'Brazil', tz: -3, peak: 100 },
];
const P_BLIP = 0.004, P_FAIL = 0.9, BLOCK = 0.12;
const LCP_MEDIAN = 1700, LCP_SIGMA = 0.45, FAULT_FACTOR = 3, POOR = 4000;
const RUM_WINDOW = 15, RUM_LAG = 3, RUM_MIN = 20, RUM_HOLD = 3;
const MIN_PER_H = 60, HOURS_PER_DAY = 24;
const PEAK_HOUR = 20, NIGHT_FLOOR = 0.1; // local hour of peak traffic; traffic share left at the quietest hour
const Z_SD = 0.5774; // standard deviation of the sum of four uniforms (approximate normal draw)
const LATE_SYNTH_MIN = 15; // a synthetic alert later than this into the fault is blamed on a coincident blip
const CHART = { x0: 10, w: 700, tickH: 3 }, ROW_Y = { s: 22, r: 52 }; // timeline svg layout

function views(r: number, t: number) {
  const hour = (((t / MIN_PER_H + REGIONS[r].tz) % HOURS_PER_DAY) + HOURS_PER_DAY) % HOURS_PER_DAY;
  const c = (1 + Math.cos((2 * Math.PI * (hour - PEAK_HOUR)) / HOURS_PER_DAY)) / 2;
  return Math.round(REGIONS[r].peak * (NIGHT_FLOOR + (1 - NIGHT_FLOOR) * c * c));
}
const faulted = (scope: string, r: number, t: number) => t >= FAULT_START && t < FAULT_END && (scope === 'global' || r === BRAZIL);
function p75(a: number[]) { const s = [...a].sort((x, y) => x - y); return s[Math.ceil(0.75 * s.length) - 1]; }

function world(seed: number) {
  const g = mulberry32(seed * 977 + 13); const blip: number[][] = [], fail: number[][] = [];
  for (let r = 0; r < REGIONS.length; r++) { blip.push([]); fail.push([]); for (let t = 0; t < DAY; t++) { blip[r].push(g()); fail[r].push(g()); } }
  return { seed, blip, fail };
}
function synthetic(w: World, p: Params) {
  const L = p.locations, effN = Math.min(p.n, L), I = p.interval;
  const last: ({ bad: boolean; real: boolean } | null)[] = []; for (let k = 0; k < L; k++) last.push(null);
  let detect = -1, falseAlarms = 0, wasFalse = false, checks = 0; const marks: Mark[] = [];
  for (let t = 0; t < DAY; t++) {
    let ran = false;
    for (let k = 0; k < L; k++) {
      const off = Math.floor((k * I) / L);
      if (t >= off && (t - off) % I === 0) {
        ran = true; checks++;
        const real = faulted(p.scope, k, t) && w.fail[k][t] < P_FAIL;
        last[k] = { bad: real || w.blip[k][t] < P_BLIP, real };
      }
    }
    if (!ran) continue;
    let bad = 0, real = false;
    for (const s of last) if (s && s.bad) { bad++; if (s.real) real = true; }
    const cond = bad >= effN;
    if (cond && real && detect < 0 && t >= FAULT_START && t < FAULT_END) { detect = t; marks.push({ t, kind: 'hit' }); }
    const fa = cond && !real;
    if (fa && !wasFalse) { falseAlarms++; marks.push({ t, kind: 'false' }); }
    wasFalse = fa;
  }
  return { detect, falseAlarms, checks, marks };
}
function lcpSample(g: () => number, slow: boolean) {
  const z = ((g() + g() + g() + g() - 2) / Z_SD);
  return LCP_MEDIAN * (slow ? FAULT_FACTOR : 1) * Math.exp(LCP_SIGMA * z);
}
function rum(w: World, p: Params) {
  if (!p.rumOn) return { detect: -1, falseAlarms: 0, samples: 0, faultSamples: [], base: [], marks: [] };
  const rate = p.sampling; const perMin: number[][][] = []; let samples = 0; const faultSamples: number[] = [], base: number[] = [];
  for (let r = 0; r < REGIONS.length; r++) {
    perMin.push([]);
    for (let t = 0; t < DAY; t++) {
      const g = mulberry32(w.seed * 100003 + r * 1447 + t * 7 + 1);
      const n = Math.floor(views(r, t) * rate * (1 - BLOCK) + g());
      const slow = faulted(p.scope, r, t); const a: number[] = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) a.push(lcpSample(g, slow));
      perMin[r].push(a); samples += n;
      if (r === BRAZIL) (slow ? faultSamples : (t < FAULT_START ? base : [])).push(...a);
    }
  }
  let detect = -1, falseAlarms = 0; const marks: Mark[] = [];
  for (let r = 0; r < REGIONS.length; r++) {
    let run = 0, open = false;
    for (let t = 0; t < DAY; t++) {
      const hi = t - RUM_LAG, lo = hi - RUM_WINDOW + 1; let all: number[] = [];
      if (hi >= 0) for (let u = Math.max(0, lo); u <= hi; u++) all = all.concat(perMin[r][u]);
      const cond = all.length >= RUM_MIN && p75(all) > POOR;
      run = cond ? run + 1 : 0;
      const fire = run >= RUM_HOLD;
      if (fire && !open) {
        if (faulted(p.scope, r, t)) { if (detect < 0) { detect = t; marks.push({ t, kind: 'hit' }); } }
        else { falseAlarms++; marks.push({ t, kind: 'false' }); }
      }
      open = fire;
    }
  }
  return { detect, falseAlarms, samples, faultSamples, base, marks };
}
function simulate(p: Params) {
  const w = world(p.seed); const s = synthetic(w, p); const u = rum(w, p);
  const dets = [s.detect, u.detect].filter((x) => x >= 0); const first = dets.length ? Math.min(...dets) : -1;
  let before = 0, total = 0;
  for (let t = FAULT_START; t < FAULT_END; t++) for (let r = 0; r < REGIONS.length; r++) if (faulted(p.scope, r, t)) {
    total += views(r, t); if (first < 0 || t < first) before += views(r, t);
  }
  return { s, u, first, before, total };
}

  // ---- DOM ----
  const SVGNS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  const hhmm = (t: number) => String(Math.floor(t / MIN_PER_H)).padStart(2, '0') + ':' + String(t % MIN_PER_H).padStart(2, '0');
  const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-sm]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const mark = (svg: SVGElement, tag: string, attrs: Record<string, string>, text?: string) => {
      const e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);
      for (const k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);
      if (text !== undefined) e.textContent = text;
      svg.appendChild(e);
    };
    let frame = 0;
    function params() {
      return { seed: val('[data-seed]'), interval: val('[data-interval]'), locations: val('[data-locs]'), n: val('[data-rule]'), scope: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-scope]').value, rumOn: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rumon]').checked, sampling: val('[data-sampling]') };
    }
    function draw() {
      frame = 0;
      const p = params(); const r = simulate(p);
      q('[data-locsval]').textContent = String(p.locations);
      q('[data-locnames]').textContent = 'Probing from: ' + REGIONS.slice(0, p.locations).map((x) => x.name).join(', ') + (p.locations <= BRAZIL ? ' (none in Brazil)' : '') + '. Needs ' + Math.min(p.n, p.locations) + ' failing location' + (Math.min(p.n, p.locations) > 1 ? 's' : '') + ' to alert.';
      q<HTMLInputElement | HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sampling]').disabled = !p.rumOn;
      const after = (t: number) => '+' + (t - FAULT_START) + ' min (' + hhmm(t) + ')';
      q('[data-sdet]').textContent = r.s.detect < 0 ? 'outage never detected' : 'detected ' + after(r.s.detect);
      q('[data-sfa]').textContent = r.s.falseAlarms + ' false alarm' + (r.s.falseAlarms === 1 ? '' : 's') + ' from blips';
      q('[data-schecks]').textContent = fmt(r.s.checks) + ' probe checks in the day';
      q('[data-rdet]').textContent = !p.rumOn ? 'off' : r.u.detect < 0 ? 'outage never detected' : 'detected ' + after(r.u.detect);
      q('[data-rfa]').textContent = !p.rumOn ? 'no beacons collected' : r.u.falseAlarms + ' false alarms · ' + fmt(r.u.samples) + ' samples in the day';
      const fs = r.u.faultSamples;
      q('[data-rp75]').textContent = !p.rumOn ? 'no data' : fs.length ? 'Brazil p75 LCP in the outage: ' + fmt(Math.round(p75(fs))) + ' ms from ' + fmt(fs.length) + ' samples (good is 2,500 ms or less)' : 'no samples from the outage';
      q('[data-hurt]').textContent = fmt(r.before) + ' of ' + fmt(r.total);
      q('[data-hurtnote]').textContent = 'slow page views before the first alert' + (r.first < 0 ? ' (never alerted)' : ', ' + Math.round((100 * r.before) / r.total) + '%');
      const parts: string[] = [];
      if (r.first < 0) parts.push('Nobody was alerted. Users found out from support tickets, after the whole outage.');
      else parts.push('First alert came from ' + (r.u.detect < 0 || (r.s.detect >= 0 && r.s.detect <= r.u.detect) ? 'the synthetic probes' : 'RUM') + ' ' + (r.first - FAULT_START) + (r.first - FAULT_START === 1 ? ' minute' : ' minutes') + ' in.');
      if (p.scope === 'brazil' && r.s.detect < 0) {
        if (p.locations <= BRAZIL) parts.push('No probe runs in Brazil, so every synthetic check passed.');
        else if (Math.min(p.n, p.locations) > 1) parts.push('Only the Brazil probe fails, and the rule needs ' + Math.min(p.n, p.locations) + ' locations, so it stays quiet.');
      }
      if (p.scope === 'brazil' && r.s.detect > FAULT_START + LATE_SYNTH_MIN && Math.min(p.n, p.locations) > 1) parts.push('The synthetic alert only fired when an unrelated blip joined the Brazil failure.');
      if (p.rumOn && r.u.detect < 0 && p.scope === 'brazil') parts.push('RUM stayed silent: too few sampled page views from Brazil at night to reach ' + RUM_MIN + ' in the window.');
      if (r.s.falseAlarms > 0) parts.push(r.s.falseAlarms + ' false alarm' + (r.s.falseAlarms === 1 ? '' : 's') + ' would have woken someone for nothing.');
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = parts.join(' ');
      const svg = q<SVGElement>('[data-svg]'); svg.replaceChildren();
      const X = (t: number) => CHART.x0 + (t / DAY) * CHART.w;
      mark(svg, 'rect', { class: 'sm-band', x: String(X(FAULT_START)), y: '4', width: String(X(FAULT_END) - X(FAULT_START)), height: '66' });
      for (let h = 0; h <= HOURS_PER_DAY; h += CHART.tickH) { mark(svg, 'line', { class: 'sm-tick', x1: String(X(h * MIN_PER_H)), x2: String(X(h * MIN_PER_H)), y1: '70', y2: '75' }); mark(svg, 'text', { class: 'sm-lbl', x: String(X(h * MIN_PER_H)), y: '90', 'text-anchor': 'middle' }, String(h).padStart(2, '0')); }
      mark(svg, 'line', { class: 'sm-row', x1: '10', x2: '710', y1: String(ROW_Y.s), y2: String(ROW_Y.s) });
      mark(svg, 'line', { class: 'sm-row', x1: '10', x2: '710', y1: String(ROW_Y.r), y2: String(ROW_Y.r) });
      const dots = (marks: { t: number; kind: string }[], y: number, cls: string) => marks.forEach((m) => mark(svg, 'circle', { class: 'sm-dot ' + cls + (m.kind === 'hit' ? ' hit' : ' miss'), cx: String(X(m.t)), cy: String(y), r: m.kind === 'hit' ? '6' : '3.5' }));
      dots(r.s.marks, ROW_Y.s, 'sm-s'); dots(r.u.marks, ROW_Y.r, 'sm-r');
    }
    const schedule = () => { if (!frame) frame = requestAnimationFrame(draw); };
    root.querySelectorAll('select, input[type="range"], input[type="checkbox"]').forEach((el) => { el.addEventListener('input', schedule); el.addEventListener('change', schedule); });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-interval]').value = '5'; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-locs]').value = '3'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-rule]').value = '1';
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-scope]').value = 'brazil'; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rumon]').checked = true; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sampling]').value = '0.1'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-seed]').value = '1';
      schedule();
    });
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .sm-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .sm-chart { overflow-x: auto; }
  .playground .sm-svg { width: 100%; min-width: 420px; height: auto; display: block; }
  .playground .sm-band { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bad) 16%, transparent); stroke: var(--bad); stroke-width: 1; }
  .playground .sm-row { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .playground .sm-tick { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; }
  .playground .sm-lbl { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .playground .sm-s { stroke: var(--role-1); fill: var(--role-1); }
  .playground .sm-r { stroke: var(--role-2); fill: var(--role-2); }
  .playground .sm-dot { stroke-width: 2; }
  .playground .sm-dot.miss { fill: var(--surface); }
  .playground .sm-key { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; vertical-align: middle; }
  .playground .sm-k1 { background: var(--role-1); }
  .playground .sm-k2 { background: var(--role-2); }
</style>
